<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/general_public> dcterms:title "General Public" , "General public" ;
	linkml:description "By general users who are not necessarily AI or technical experts." , "Those most likely to experience the impacts directly, who may motivate what other AI actors do." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/governance_and_oversight> dcterms:title "Governance and Oversight" ;
	linkml:description "Holding management, fiduciary and legal authority for the organization where the system is designed, developed or deployed." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/group_or_community> dcterms:title "Group/Community" ;
	linkml:description "To a group, such as discrimination against a sub-group of a population." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/groups> dcterms:title "Groups" ;
	linkml:description "Groups of people." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/harm_to_property_communities_or_environment> dcterms:title "Harm to property, communities, or the environment" ;
	linkml:description "To things and groups beyond the individual." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/harmful_bias_or_homogenization> dcterms:title "Harmful Bias or Homogenization" ;
	skos:altLabel "Harmful Bias and Homogenization" ;
	linkml:description "Worse systemic bias, unequal performance across groups or languages, and output skewed by sameness." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/human_ai> dcterms:title "Human / AI" ;
	linkml:description "By GAI together with human teams, specialist or not." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/human_ai_configuration> dcterms:title "Human-AI Configuration" ;
	skos:altLabel "Human AI Configuration" ;
	linkml:description "Interaction that leads people to over-rely on, anthropomorphize or become entangled with a system, or to distrust it." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/human_ai_interaction> dcterms:title "Human-AI interaction" ;
	linkml:description "How a person and a system act on each other." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/human_authentication> dcterms:title "Human authentication" ;
	linkml:description "Having people confirm where content came from." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/human_baseline> dcterms:title "Human baseline" ;
	linkml:description "A system that augments or replaces human activity needs a baseline, which is hard to systematize." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/human_behavior> dcterms:title "Human behavior" ;
	linkml:description "Abuse, misuse or unsafe repurposing by people, whether adversarial or not." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/human_cognitive> dcterms:title "Human-cognitive" ;
	linkml:description "In how people perceive system information to decide, or think about what a system is for." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/human_factors> dcterms:title "Human Factors" ;
	linkml:description "Human-centered design and evaluation, involving end users and bringing context-specific norms and values into design." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/impact_assessments> dcterms:title "Impact assessments" .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/incident_response> dcterms:title "Incident response" .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/individual> dcterms:title "Individual" ;
	linkml:description "To a person's civil liberties, rights, safety or economic opportunity." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/individuals> dcterms:title "Individuals" ;
	linkml:description "Particular people." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/information_integrity> dcterms:title "Information Integrity" ;
	linkml:description "Easier creation and spread of content that blurs fact and opinion, or that can drive large disinformation campaigns." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/information_security> dcterms:title "Information Security" ;
	linkml:description "Easier offensive cyber activity, and a larger attack surface on a system, its data, code or weights." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/informing> dcterms:title "Informing audience" ;
	linkml:description "AI actors in the People and Planet dimension, who inform the primary audience." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/injury_or_harm_to_health> dcterms:title "Injury or harm to health" ;
	linkml:description "To a person or group, including psychological harm and harm to mental health." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/inputs> dcterms:title "Inputs" ;
	linkml:description "What goes into the model or system." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/inscrutability> dcterms:title "Inscrutability" ;
	linkml:description "Opaque systems, poor documentation and inherent uncertainty complicate measurement." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-ai-rmf/integer> a linkml:TypeDefinition ;
	skos:editorialNote "If you are authoring schemas in LinkML YAML, the type is referenced with the lower case \"integer\"." ;
